# Controls what EAS Build uploads. MUST live at the git repository root — eas-cli looks for
# it at `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, not next to app.json. A copy inside mobile/ is
# silently ignored.
#
# IMPORTANT: when this file exists, eas-cli does NOT read any .gitignore (root, backend/,
# mobile/, frontend/). Every rule below has to be repeated here or the file gets uploaded.
# The upload is the whole repo (`tar` runs at the git root), so backend/ is in scope too.
#
# The one deliberate omission is mobile/google-services.json: it must stay out of git but
# must reach the builder, or the APK ships with no Firebase config and push silently never
# works. Uploading it is safe — it is client configuration embedded in every APK you ship,
# not a secret. The real secret is backend/firebase-service-account.json, excluded below.

# ── Not needed for an Android build; excluded so backend secrets can never ride along ──
# Leading slash anchors to the repo root, so this cannot accidentally match a directory
# named "backend" nested somewhere inside mobile/src.
/backend
/frontend

# ── Secrets (mirrors the .gitignore rules that no longer apply) ──
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
firebase-service-account.json
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
*serviceAccount*.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# Signing material must never leave your machine
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
*.mobileprovision

# ── Dependencies and build output — regenerated on the build server ──
# Bare name, no trailing slash: a "node_modules/" pattern only matches when the path is
# known to be a directory, which is not how every check evaluates it.
node_modules
/mobile/.expo
/mobile/dist
/mobile/web-build
/mobile/ios
/mobile/android
/mobile/.kotlin
/mobile/expo-env.d.ts

# ── Editor / OS noise ──
.idea
.vscode
*.iml
.DS_Store
*.log
*.local
*.tsbuildinfo
*.orig.*

# NOTE: mobile/google-services.json is deliberately NOT listed — it must be uploaded.
